Q: Vue.js dynamic &lt;style&gt; with variables A: <h1>Vue 3 State-Driven Dynamic CSS Variables</h1>
<p>I know this is a bit late and is using Vue.js 2, but as of now in Vue.js 3 you can create state-driven CSS variables.</p>
<p>You can now use your SFC (Single File Component) state data inside your styles tags using <code>v-bind()</code>.</p>
<p>You can read more about state-driven CSS variables <a href="https://www.jsnow.io/javascript/vue/vue-dynamic-css" rel="nofollow noreferrer">here</a>, or read the Vue.js 3 documentation <a href="https://v3.vuejs.org/api/sfc-style.html#state-driven-dynamic-css" rel="nofollow noreferrer">here</a>.</p>
<p>Here is a code example</p>
<h4>Example</h4>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;template&gt;
  &lt;div&gt;
    &lt;input type=&quot;text&quot; v-model=&quot;color&quot; /&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;user-input-color&quot;&gt;
      {{ color }}
    &lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/template&gt;

&lt;script&gt;
export default {
  data: () =&gt; ({
    color: 'white'
  })
}
&lt;/script&gt;

&lt;style scoped&gt;
.user-input-color {
  background-color: v-bind('color')
}
&lt;/style&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>Here is a link to the <a href="https://vue-state-driven-css-variables-example.vercel.app/" rel="nofollow noreferrer">live example</a>.</p>
